description:
FILED s473t4 (#1501 CHECK 1 round 1, 2026-09-13).  t/comp/our.t is TRANSPILE-FAIL: P 7/0, C 0/0 -- the whole file.

    $ ./pl2cl < t/comp/our.t
    Parser2 TODO: our '$y' shadows a my-lexical

THE SITE, t/comp/our.t:68-73:
    $y = 1;
    {
        my $y = 2;
        {
            our $y = $y;
            is($y, 2, 'our shouldnt be visible until introduced')

MINIMAL REPRODUCER (probed vs perl 5.40.3):
    use strict; use warnings;
    our $y;
    $y = 1;
    { my $y = 2;
      { our $y = $y;
        print "inner=$y\n"; } }
    print "outer=$main::y\n";
    perl: "our" variable $y redeclared at ... line 7.   (a warning)
                  (Did you mean "local" instead of "our"?)
          inner=2
          outer=2
    pcl : Transpile failed: Parser2 TODO: our '$y' shadows a my-lexical

PERL'S RULE, and the point of the test: an `our $y = EXPR` introduces the package alias AFTER the statement, so the `$y` on the RIGHT is still the enclosing `my $y` (2).  The assignment therefore writes 2 into $main::y, and the inner block's `$y` reads the package alias (also 2).  The whole file is seven rows testing exactly this ordering.

PCL refuses the shape outright.  It is the same "a declaration is not visible inside its own statement" rule as #1582 -- one rule, two refusals, two whole files (7 + 106 rows).  Consider fixing them together.

Round t5c (comp/).
